# Context

## Background
The owner pushed three commits from another machine on 2026-11-25
(20:08 to 20:31) while four local commits waited for a push. The owner
asked for a pull.

## Why This Way
A merge keeps the four local commits and their notes. A rebase would
write new hashes for each of them and drop their notes, because
notes.rewrite.rebase is not set here. The repository has merge
commits before. The pull used --no-rebase --no-commit, so the full
check ran on the merged tree before this commit. Result: exit 0,
37 packages.

## Gotchas
- git pull without a strategy fails on this repository, because no
  pull.rebase is set and the branches diverged.
- Both sides changed DB.md and NOTES.md. git merged them without a
  conflict; the merged passages were read before the commit.
